# N21 q07 disclosure repair review

Reviewer: `independent_agent`, `codex-independent-N21-review-20261122-FIRST`.
This is the same reviewer's affected-only continuation, not a fresh content,
mathematical or figure review.

Substantive verdict: **PASS** for this disclosure repair. The FIRST review's
REVISE finding required explicit loss disclosure and a narrowed task claim, or
actual source-graph discrimination. The parent chose disclosure, and all five
changed fields implement that permitted resolution:

- `q07.intent.task`: explicitly uses the supplied original graph and excludes
  original arrow-to-point inference from assessment.
- `q07.intent.unit_reason`: says the complete original graph is equal in every
  option; identifies full coordinate reversal, axis-reflection discrimination and
  both functionhood judgments as the assessed task.
- `q07.intent.limitations`: keeps the plotting loss and explicitly adds supplied,
  unassessed reading/construction of the original five-point set.
- `coverage.428.omitted_tasks`: adds original arrow-to-point inference as supplied
  and unassessed, alongside the retained plotting loss.
- `coverage.428.reason`: no longer treats author/reviewer image observations as
  proof of learner arrow reading; narrows coverage to the inverse full point set
  versus axis reflection and both functionhood decisions.

The loss has been declared, not restored. The remaining inverse task was already
substantively accepted in the FIRST blind review; this disposition does not
weaken an essential source or mathematics standard.

